James inquired about his rights regarding a solar contractor, Green Home Systems (GHS), who had not completed a project over a year after signing a contract that estimated completion within six months. He sought to understand if he could declare GHS in breach of contract and how to compel them to finish the work. The assistant clarified that GHS could be in material breach based on the extensive delay. James was advised to send a formal notice of breach, allowing GHS a defined period to cure the issues. Additionally, he was instructed to compile documentation and maintain his obligations while waiting for GHS’s response. If GHS failed to comply, he should consult a lawyer to explore termination and further remedies.
